<title>USA: CME November volume slips 7.4 pct from year ago.</title>
<headline>CME November volume slips 7.4 pct from year ago.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange (CME) said volume in November totalled 12,525,453 contracts, down 7.4 percent from the year-earlier level of 13,532,532 contracts.</p>
<p>Open interest at month's end stood at 6,853,768, up 10.4 percent from 6,205,764 at the end of November last year.</p>
<p>Year-to-date volume totalled 182,571,223, off 3.1 percent from 188,323,319 traded during the first 11 months of last year.  </p>
<p>Major categories were as follows:</p>
<p>Futures (individual)   Nov 1996	% change	 Nov 1995</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   5,600,618	  -16.6	   6,716,090</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   461,311	   +1.0	     456,749</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   388,568	   -4.7	     407,842</p>
<p>  Swiss franc	    340,097	   +9.3	     311,200</p>
<p>  British pound	  184,164	   -3.9	     191,694</p>
<p>  Canadian dollar	   194,050     +99.7		97,156</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		1,459,123	   -1.6	   1,483,007</p>
<p>  Live cattle	    312,868	  +26.8	     246,765</p>
<p>  Live/lean hogs	 171,003	  +20.0	     142,493</p>
<p>Options on futures</p>
<p>  Eurodollar	   1,435,999	  -11.1	   1,615,456</p>
<p>  Eurodollar midcurve     313,076	 +210.9	     100,687</p>
<p>  British pound	   82,486	  -66.0	     242,355</p>
<p>  Deutschemark	   176,222	   +1.7	     173,245</p>
<p>  Japanese yen	   163,035	   +1.5	     160,632</p>
<p>  S&amp;P 500		  446,772	  -17.5	     541,357</p>
<p>  Live cattle	     48,014	  +42.9		33,598</p>
<p>Since January 1994 CME has counted in volume anything that creates or liquidates open positions including expired options and SIMEX mutual offset transactions cleared on the CME.</p>
<p>Excluding these transactions, CME &quot;pit traded&quot; volume for November 1996 totaled 125,525,453 and year-to-date volume stood at 182,571,223.</p>
<p>-- Chicago Derivatives Desk (312) 408-8750</p>
